"/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Primary reading</div><h1>Four papers. Explicit claim boundaries.</h1><p class="lede">Current review editions from the living portal, preserved with their versions. Publication distributes a result; it does not complete independent review.</p></div><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">I</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper I · 1.1.1</span><h2>Finite carriers and support flow</h2><p>Finite Tetrahedral Complexes, Skew Support Flow and Contact Readiness</p><p class="muted">Finite carriers, skew flow, unique-simplex gluing, spectra, ambient jumps and supplied readiness.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PI">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">II</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper II · 1.1.1</span><h2>Projective reconstruction</h2><p>Projective Reconstruction, Complex Phase Receipts and Frozen-Tree Validation</p><p class="muted">Real and complex phase receipts, parity ambiguities, frozen-tree validation and covariance.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_II_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PII">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_II_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">III</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper III · 1.1.1</span><h2>Symmetry, shells and collective mechanisms</h2><p>Tetrahedral Symmetry, Radial Spectra and Finite Collective Mechanisms</p><p class="muted">Signed symmetry, radial shells, prepared shapes, burden, retention and collective mechanisms.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_III_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PIII">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_III_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row"><div class="paper-number">IV</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Paper IV · 0.1</span><h2>Prepared controllers and renewal</h2><p>Finite Prepared Quantum Controllers, Capture Windows and Correlation-Preserving Renewal</p><p class="muted">Finite apparatus, history clocks, capture windows, joint errors and correlation-preserving renewal.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_IV_REVIEW_DRAFT_v0.1.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=PIV">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_PAPER_IV_REVIEW_DRAFT_v0.1.md" download>Markdown ↓</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="higher-rank-curved-v01"><div class="paper-number">G8</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>The embedded curved branch at every finite rank</h2><p>New color directions preserve the upper endpoint and expose a zero-stiffness exception.</p><p class="muted">For r≥2 the specified one-active-color orbit is nonlinearly stable exactly for 0&lt;κ≤rκ*(N), where κ*/N≈0.03760248457. Active-to-unused color modes have positive restoring energy and a vanishing magnetic Hessian. At κ=0 an unused color permits exact holonomy drift; above the upper boundary active scalar instability embeds. The residual U(r-1) Gauss condition is retained. 57 exact checks and two full matrix nonlinear campaigns; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/higher-rank-curved-v0.1/UD_HIGHER_RANK_CURVED_STABILITY_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/higher-rank-curved-v0.1/UD_HIGHER_RANK_CURVED_STABILITY_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=HRC01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="curved-modes-v01"><div class="paper-number">G7</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Curved modes and the sharp scalar boundary</h2><p>42 reduced mode pairs and a stable critical endpoint.</p><p class="muted">At fixed equal species norms the scalar reduction has 84 real dimensions: 14 neutral matter pairs and 28 link–charge pairs. Exact weighted stiffness gives κ*/N≈0.03760248457, improving the previous sufficient bound. The orbit is nonlinearly stable through equality and unstable above it. At equality, three zero Jordan chains coexist with stability because an exact integer interval certificate proves positive quartic restoring energy. 47 exact checks and three numerical campaigns; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/curved-modes-v0.1/UD_CURVED_REDUCED_MODES_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/curved-modes-v0.1/UD_CURVED_REDUCED_MODES_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=CRM01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="curved-ground-v01"><div class="paper-number">G6</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>A stable nonzero curved matter orbit</h2><p>The unchanged action admits a stable scalar background with negative diamond holonomy.</p><p class="muted">Links U=-ib and positive lowest-mode matter give an exactly neutral relative equilibrium. At scalar rank, a constrained energy proof establishes nonlinear orbital stability for an explicit positive stiffness interval. A separate finite-rank theorem guarantees a stable minimizing set and forces nonflat minima at sufficiently small κ/(rN). Individual-orbit stability at higher rank remains open. 40 exact checks and two numerical campaigns; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/curved-ground-v0.1/UD_CURVED_GROUND_STABILITY_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/curved-ground-v0.1/UD_CURVED_GROUND_STABILITY_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=CGS01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="resonance-closure-v01"><div class="paper-number">G5</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>All six resonant cases closed</h2><p>Exact symmetry sectors complete the nonlinear instability theorem.</p><p class="muted">An S3 vertex-stabilizer sector and a C4 cyclic sector provide exactly Gauss-admissible, fixed-norm nonlinear departure witnesses at the six formerly excluded values. Together with the preceding proof, the specified nonzero neutral flat family is unstable for every a&gt;0 and κ≥0 at finite rank. 104 exact constructor checks and six numerical campaigns; independent review pending; unchanged candidate action; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/resonance-closure-v0.1/UD_RESONANCE_CLOSURE_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/resonance-closure-v0.1/UD_RESONANCE_CLOSURE_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=RSC01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="nonlinear-orbital-v01"><div class="paper-number">G4</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Nonlinear orbital instability</h2><p>Finite matter departure from arbitrarily small admissible perturbations.</p><p class="muted">An additional conserved Gram matrix and a force-canceling sector enable a controlled averaging proof. The nonzero neutral flat family is nonlinearly orbitally unstable within the unchanged candidate action except at six positive parameter values left open. The zero-matter vacuum stability theorem is preserved. 42 exact constructor checks; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/nonlinear-orbital-v0.1/UD_NONLINEAR_ORBITAL_INSTABILITY_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/nonlinear-orbital-v0.1/UD_NONLINEAR_ORBITAL_INSTABILITY_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=NOI01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="gauge-reduced-modes-v01"><div class="paper-number">G3</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Gauge-reduced modes and stability</h2><p>Exact mode frequencies, persistent Jordan chains, and a stable vacuum gauge orbit.</p><p class="muted">The nonzero neutral flat family has 86 real reduced dimensions in the Abelian branch. Its imaginary spectrum retains nongauge secular growth for every positive diamond stiffness. A separate conserved-functional proof establishes nonlinear vacuum stability. Higher-rank slice modes retain their residual stabilizer constraint. Candidate action; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/gauge-reduced-modes-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_REDUCED_MODES_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gauge-reduced-modes-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_REDUCED_MODES_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=GRM01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="joint-hamiltonian-v01"><div class="paper-number">G2</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Gauss closure and reciprocal dynamics</h2><p>A constrained joint link–matter Hamiltonian with an exact neutral curvature seed.</p><p class="muted">A declared classical U(r) action preserves matrix Gauss law, total energy and both matter norms, with global temporal-gauge flow. A dynamical opposite-charge partner admits nonzero neutral initial states. Their backreaction can leave the flat-link sector. Action and species selection, physical group and correspondence remain open. Physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/joint-hamiltonian-v0.1/UD_JOINT_HAMILTONIAN_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/joint-hamiltonian-v0.1/UD_JOINT_HAMILTONIAN_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=GHT01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="gauge-transport-v01"><div class="paper-number">G1</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Gauge-covariant incidence transport</h2><p>A flatness theorem and an exact phase-controlled spectrum.</p><p class="muted">Unitary transport on the 28 Hasse links preserves support and gauge covariance. Retaining the transport chain identity forces flatness on the filled tetrahedron. A one-link phase gives a conditional spectral splitting. Source-selected group, gauge-field action, continuum and physical correspondence remain open.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/gauge-transport-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_TRANSPORT_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gauge-transport-v0.1/UD_GAUGE_TRANSPORT_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Proof and replay package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=GBT01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article><article class="paper-row" id="narrative-v015"><div class="paper-number">N</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Additional workstream · review candidate 0.15</span><h2>Distinction, interaction and persistence</h2><p>A separate 56-page theoretical synthesis by Benjamin Walker Mayes, dated 15 October 2026 UTC.</p><p class="muted">Ingested source: gluing and dynamic memory, noisy access, finite records, sampled events and receipt-error limits. Its claims retain their stated assumptions; companion replay packages were not supplied for this intake. Independent review remains pending. Physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/narrative-v0.15/UD_Theory_Narrative_Manuscript_v0.15.pdf">Read PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=N015">Source and scope →</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/narrative-v0.15/INTAKE_v0.1.md">Intake receipt ↓</a></div></div></article><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>Reproduction and review.</h2><p>Every imported source retains its own constructor-check record. The new atlas additionally verifies three core incidence constructions with exact arithmetic; that check is limited to boundary identities, skew symmetry, spectra and simplex counts.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/sources/UD_ATLAS_CORE_VERIFICATION_v0.1.json">Atlas check receipt ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/verify_core.py" download>Exact checker ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/papers/UD_Exact_Reproduction_v1.0_2026-09-16.zip" download>Earlier exact reproduction package ↓</a></div><p class="muted">The earlier v1.0 package is retained as an earlier replay object, not relabeled as a full verifier for the later papers.</p></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public reading edition 0.14</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
